hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"968","**\nNarrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la, who said: Ibn Wahb informed us, that Malik informed him, from Abu az-Zubayr al-Makki, from Abu at-Tufayl 'Amir ibn Wathilah, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal informed him that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the year of Tabuk. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would combine the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers, and the Maghrib and 'Isha' prayers.\n\nHe said: One day, he delayed the prayer, then went out and prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together. Then he entered, then went out and prayed Maghrib and 'Isha' together. Then he said: \Verily"," you will come tomorrow"," if Allah wills"," to the spring of Tabuk. You will not reach it until the day has advanced. Whoever reaches it"," let him not touch any of its water until I come.\""\n\nHe said: So we came to it"," and two men had already preceded us to it. The spring was like a sandal-strap"," trickling with a little water. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked the two men: \""Did you touch any of its water?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So he rebuked them and said what Allah willed him to say.\n\nThen they scooped from the spring with their hands until some water had gathered in something. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) washed his face and hands in it"," then returned it to the spring"," whereupon the spring gushed forth with abundant water. The people drew water"," then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""It is imminent"," O Mu'adh"," if your life is prolonged"," that you will see what is here filled with gardens.\""\n\nAbu Bakr said: In this narration"," what is clear and established is that the Prophet (ﷺ) combined Zuhr and 'Asr"," and Maghrib and 'Isha'"," while he was staying in his journey"," not traveling at the time of combining the two prayers. For his statement"," \""He delayed the prayer one day"," then went out and prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together. Then he entered"," then went out and prayed Maghrib and 'Isha' together","\"" clarifies that he was not traveling during these two times in which he combined the Maghrib and 'Isha'"," and the Zuhr and 'Asr.\n\nThe narration of Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ)"," when the journey became pressing"," would combine the two prayers"," is not in contradiction to this narration. For Ibn 'Umar saw the Prophet (ﷺ) combine the two prayers when the journey became pressing"," so he reported what he saw the Prophet (ﷺ) do. And Mu'adh ibn Jabal saw the Prophet (ﷺ) combine the two prayers while he was staying at a place"," not traveling"," so he reported what he saw the Prophet (ﷺ) do.\n\nThus"," combining the two prayers when the journey becomes pressing for the traveler is permissible"," as the Prophet (ﷺ) did. Likewise"," it is permissible for him to combine them even if he is staying and the journey is not pressing"," as the Prophet (ﷺ) did. And Ibn 'Umar did not say that combining the two prayers is not permissible if the journey is not pressing. There is no narration from the Prophet (ﷺ) to that effect"," nor did he report it from himself."""
